From e85b1cbff9b691c54877421c32a576c0da3c37c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:36:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Clock from HTTP with time zone and the DSi's clock chip;
 fewer idle shells; TERMINFO

- w99b on the console: ntpclient never got an answer (NTP blocked on the
  guest network) and stayed resident; date said 2016. httpdate: the time
  from a web server's Date header (HTTP 80); -z the time zone from where
  the network is (worldtimeapi.org, then ip-api.com; IANA name mapped to
  a POSIX TZ for uClibc; skipped with /etc/config/TZ.manual); -w the
  local time into the DSi's clock chip; -L at boot (rc): the chip holds
  local time, the kernel took it as UTC. The Wi-Fi window runs
  httpdate -z -s -w after a successful DHCP instead of ntpclient.
- The clock chip: NDS_SD_CMD_RTC (ARM7, sdmmc.c): the DS RTC protocol
  of arm7/time.c (command bit 7 first, data bit 0 first) with a busy
  loop instead of swiDelay (SD requests run in the IRQ handler), 24/12 h
  mode from status register 1; dsisd_rtc(); /proc/dsisettings
  "rtc YYYY MM DD WD hh mm ss".
- memreport (w99b) showed six msh shells of about 400 KB: dsautolog
  (C) replaces the /boot/autolog loop (a shell plus a resident sleep,
  ~650 KB, and savelog every 10 s); it runs savelog only when the
  kernel log or a log file changed, or every 5 min. The boot session
  execs /boot/desktop in place of the login shell, and the desktop
  script execs a shell when the desktop ends. The SSH server window
  closes on Enter instead of keeping a shell.
- nano: the DSi's ncurses has no default terminfo directory, so the
  installed descriptions were not found: nxterm sets
  TERMINFO=/usr/share/terminfo (and the profile does, scripts side).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
